# Intel RealSense D435I – PointCloud Filters (ROS2 Humble, ARM/NEON)

from : https://github.com/realsenseai/realsense-ros

Tested with:
- Intel RealSense D435I
- ROS2 Humble
- realsense2_camera driver
- ARM (NEON build, e.g. Jetson)

---

## ⚠ Important for ARM / NEON Users

On ARM platforms, the correct parameter name is:

    pointcloud__neon_.enable

NOT:

    pointcloud.enable

If the launch argument does not activate it, enable it after startup:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera pointcloud__neon_.enable true

---

# Minimal Working Setup

Launch:

    ros2 launch realsense2_camera rs_launch.py \
        align_depth.enable:=true \
        pointcloud__neon_.enable:=true

If pointcloud still does not publish:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera pointcloud__neon_.enable true

Check:

    ros2 topic list | grep points

---

# Remove 2m Distance Cutoff

Check current clipping:

    ros2 param get /camera/camera clip_distance

Disable clipping:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera clip_distance -1.0

Or increase max distance:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera clip_distance 5.0

Default D435I range:
~0.2m to ~10m (depends on lighting & texture)

---

# PointCloud Filters

## 1️⃣ Spatial Filter (Reduce Spatial Noise)

Smooths neighboring pixels to reduce local noise.

Enable:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera spatial_filter.enable true

Tune:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera spatial_filter.filter_magnitude 2
    ros2 param set /camera/camera spatial_filter.filter_smooth_alpha 0.5
    ros2 param set /camera/camera spatial_filter.filter_smooth_delta 20

Tuning Notes:
- filter_magnitude: 1–5 (higher = smoother, less detail)
- filter_smooth_alpha: 0.4–0.8 (higher = more smoothing)
- filter_smooth_delta: 10–50 (edge preservation)

Recommended balanced value:
    filter_magnitude = 2

---

## 2️⃣ Temporal Filter (Reduce Flickering)

Stabilizes depth between consecutive frames.

Enable:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera temporal_filter.enable true

Tune:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera temporal_filter.filter_smooth_alpha 0.4
    ros2 param set /camera/camera temporal_filter.filter_smooth_delta 20

Best used when camera is static.

Higher alpha = more smoothing but more latency.

---

## 3️⃣ Decimation Filter (Reduce Resolution)

Reduces point density for better performance.

Enable:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera decimation_filter.enable true

Tune:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera decimation_filter.filter_magnitude 8

Magnitude effect:
- 2 → half resolution
- 4 → quarter resolution

Use for embedded systems or SLAM speed optimization.

---

## 4️⃣ Hole Filling Filter

Fills missing depth pixels (useful for smoother surfaces).

Enable:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera hole_filling_filter.enable true

Optional tuning:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera hole_filling_filter.holes_fill 1

Modes:
- 0 = disabled
- 1 = fill from nearest
- 2 = fill from farthest

---

## 5️⃣ Laser Power (Improves Depth Quality)

Increase IR projector power:

    ros2 param set /camera/camera depth_module.laser_power 360

Max value for D435I: 360

Higher value = better depth at longer distances (more power consumption).

---

# Recommended Balanced Profile

    ros2 param set /camera/camera align_depth.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera pointcloud__neon_.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera spatial_filter.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera temporal_filter.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera hole_filling_filter.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera clip_distance -1.0

---

# Performance Profile (Jetson / ARM)

    ros2 param set /camera/camera pointcloud__neon_.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera decimation_filter.enable true
    ros2 param set /camera/camera decimation_filter.filter_magnitude 2
    ros2 param set /camera/camera temporal_filter.enable true

---

# Debug Commands

Check pointcloud frame:

    ros2 topic echo /camera/camera/depth/color/points --once

Check frequency:

    ros2 topic hz /camera/camera/depth/color/points

List parameters:

    ros2 param list /camera/camera

